{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>גם אני.</b> בתעלוליהם from the pattern of עלילות דברים (Deuteronomy 22:17), and the meaning is the false charge that will come upon them, or from the pattern of ויתעללו בה (Judges 19:25), להתעולל (1 Samuel 6:6):" "<b>ומגורתם.</b> Their fear, like ויגר מואב (Numbers 22:3):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra proposes two possible derivations for בתעלוליהם; the Hebrew lemma and proof-texts are preserved in Hebrew script per discipline, as the argument turns on lexical forms.", 1 "Resolved יראת׳ as יראתם based on context; the apostrophe in the source marks an abbreviation or suspended final letter."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:11.312190664Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}